    "turn_text": "I disagree with them. The policies put in place by Illinois, high taxes, high crime. You know, lack of a good business climate continues to cause people to leave Illinois. We continue to hemorrhage people out of this state because of the policy. Now, I would just say it's not just Illinois as a blue state with these policies. Look at New York, look at New Jersey, look at Connecticut. High tax states got lots of issues with crime. Look at California. People are leaving California. Where are the states that people are going? They're going to places like Florida, Tennessee, Texas, Georgia, where you have policymakers, particularly governors and state legislators that have done just the opposite. Florida doesn't have any income tax, right? They want to keep it that way. They have the lowest crime rate in Florida in 50 years. They continue to have one of the best economies in the country. I disagree with my colleagues. And look at the new mayor we elected in Chicago, who has doubled down on, you know, progressivism, defunding police, taxing people that make over 100,000 in Chicago. You know, you're going to continue to have people leaving the state with the policies that Democrats have continued to double down on.",
