    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46687.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "You know, I think we're seeing that divided government is forcing a Biden administration to take a hard look at spending cuts. We're $32 trillion in debt. We got to figure out how we reduce spending in this country. You know, so I view that in companion with the debt ceiling now. I'm not one that believes that we can default on our debts. We will have a catastrophic effect on our economy and jobs and people that I represent. That shouldn't happen. But we are having a conversation. We pass the bill in the House that does both of those things. We can chew gum and walk at the same time. Figure out a package of spending reductions. We're putting work requirements on welfare recipients. We're capping spending at 2022 levels. We're also looking at how we claw back some of the COVID money. I mean, these are all common sense things in trying to do that in a bipartisan way to do that. And I feel good about where we're at right now. But with divided government, we'll see what happens. We're negotiating. And I don't want to go up to the very edge of defaulting. But we're going to be doing this negotiation for probably another week to 10 days.",
