    "turn_text": "The way it translated, every one of my constituents back home has to meet a monthly budget. Every business has to meet a budget. Every city and municipality has to meet a budget. Other government has been able to do that. When we pass the bill eventually to raise the debt, along with spending cuts, what's that going to do with? It's going to help reduce inflation. because we have way too high of inflation. But it's also going to calm the markets and show that we're we as Republicans. This is something we ran on, fiscal responsibility, fiscal discipline, and bringing down the cost of living that has gone up in this country, but also reversing the trend on all the money that we've spent. And so we're finally, as Republicans, doing what we said we were going to do is exercising fiscal vanity, fiscal responsibility, and holding the Biden administration accountable.",
