  {
    "episode_id": 46687,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46687.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Again, Congressman Darren LaHood, a conversation I had with him yesterday about a variety of things and moving from the debt ceiling debate to the Durham reports took four years, millions of dollars. It's all about the genesis of the Trump-Russia collusion investigation that the FBI launched using foreign intelligence surveillance act warrants to get the authority to essentially spy on suspects or subjects in the Trump campaign and then the Trump administration. So obviously a lot of people were waiting for that report. Congressman LaHood being one of those waiting for that report. Here's his reaction to what the details were coming out of that.",
