  {
    "episode_id": 46687,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46687.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Well, we didn't get the prosecutions we wanted or the ones that actually put people in jail. But I think what the Durham probe shows, I mean, shows a disturbing pattern that's really unacceptable in the federal government. It confirms that there were serious errors at shortcomings, obviously with the FBI and their probe in the alleged connections between the Russian government and the Trump campaign during the 2016 presidential election. That is very apparent here. It confirms that the FBI repeatedly disregarded critical protections that safeguard Americans from unlawful surveillance. That was in there. And there must be accountability and reform at the FBI. Now, having said that, Greg, I'm a former federal prosecutor, I believe that there are good people that work within the FBI and DOJ. And I will also say, all of the things in the Durham report happened under Obama's FBI Director, who was Jim Comey. And so there have been reforms and changes made since Jim Comey left. And so the Durham report highlights the mistakes made by Comey and the distrust that many people have. We, as Republicans have taken over, have taken the initiative of bringing significant reforms to the FBI. I think you'll see that when we have a Pfizer reauthorization bill that will come forth where we're really gutting the authority that the FBI has. uh... and making sure that uh... uh... they're held accountable and that there's punitive and criminal measures in place uh... to help to turn the type of activity that happened uh... under obama's fbi director",
