  {
    "episode_id": 46687,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46687.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Well, we were pleased as part of our Lincoln Day dinner last Friday night to welcome Governor DeSantis to Peoria. We have record crowd, 1300 people there, biggest crowd ever. He gave a terrific speech, was well received by everybody there. Obviously, he didn't make any announcement on running for president, but he talked about the model in Florida and what he's been able to do. And it's really been remarkable what he's been able to do in terms of turning around the state of Florida, building up more Republicans in the state legislature there. His track record on the economy, on crime, on going after wokeism and cancel culture, fixing the education system. I mean, lots of things, how he navigated COVID. So I think it's a real example. He highlighted that and talked about that. We'll see what happens. Obviously, he hasn't announced yet. I think people anticipate that he will. You know, we're going to have a strong field of candidates out there. I haven't made any decisions on an endorsement yet. Greg, I still think it's early on this, but I served with Governor DeSantis. I like him, and I think he's got a tremendous record of leading. And the last point that I will make is I want a winner. I want someone that can win someone that has a track record of winning and can help us keep the majority in the house and win all across the country.",
